==About==
===Format===
* '''Swiss Stage:''' February ''28<sup>th</sup>'' -  March ''4<sup>th</sup>'', 2026
** 8-team Swiss System Format
*** 2<sup>nd</sup> and 3<sup>rd</sup> place teams from the International Leagues
** All matches are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
** {{Bgcolortext|up|Top 4 teams}} proceed to ''Playoffs''
** {{Bgcolortext|down|Bottom 4 teams}} are eliminated
** <span class="mw-customtoggle-Swiss-Draw" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for detailed information about the Swiss Stage Draw''</span>
<div class="table-responsive">
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-Swiss-Draw" style="margin-top:10px;" style="margin-left:45px;">
* '''Round 1:'''
** Second-seeded team is matched against a third-seeded team from a different region
*** Pool 1: EMEA ''#2'', Americas ''#2'', Pacific ''#2'', China ''#2''
*** Pool 2: EMEA ''#3'', Americas ''#3'', Pacific ''#3'', China ''#3''
* '''Round 2 & 3:'''
** Intra-regional matchups are permitted
** Matches are seeded based on each team's win-loss record
** For Round 3, repeat matchups from previous rounds are not allowed
</div></div>

* '''Playoffs:''' March ''6<sup>th</sup>'' - ''15<sup>th</sup>'', 2026
** 8-team Double-Elimination bracket
*** 4 teams from the ''Swiss Stage''
*** The 4 winners from each International League
** All matches ''(excl. Lower Bracket Final and Grand Final)'' are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
** Lower Bracket Final and Grand Final are {{Abbr/Bo5}}
** <span class="mw-customtoggle-Playoffs-Draw" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for detailed information about the Playoffs Draw''</span>
<div class="table-responsive">
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-Playoffs-Draw" style="margin-top:10px;" style="margin-left:45px;">
* Top-seeded teams pick their Upper Bracket Quarterfinal opponents from the Swiss Stage teams in random order
<!--** Order drawn: [[XLG Esports]], then [[Rex Regum Qeon]], then [[G2 Esports]], leaving [[Fnatic]] with the last remaining Swiss Stage qualifier
** Picks were done live at the Enercare Centre with {{Abbr|Victoria Horsley|Global Competition Manager of VALORANT}}, [[Vansilli]] and representatives from each top seed after the conclusion of the Swiss Stage-->
</div></div>

* '''Skirmish Side Selection:''' <ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ValorantEsports/status/2011453254891110603|title=Starting at Kickoff, equally seeded VCT matches will use a skill-based standard for side selection.|date=2026-01-14|author=[[Riot Games]]}}</ref>
** Applies to all matches ''(excl. Swiss Round 1, {{Abbr|UB|Upper Bracket}} Round 1, {{Abbr|LB|Lower Bracket}} Round 2 & {{Abbr|LB|Lower Bracket}} Final)''
** Before the start of a match, each team submits a starting player to represent the team
** The two players face off in a 1v1 in the in-game [[Skirmish]] game mode
** Abilities are disabled, only guns can be used
** First player to reach five rounds wins the Skirmish
** Winner player grants their team the choice to be the starting team or the second team in the Map Veto

